{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1793340958563562668,"compiled_state":{"alias":"moonstone-cut-eft","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":0,"unsigned":1},"authorship_ledger":[],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1793330513687436001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Observation\nReported downstream (nava-rebar 0.13.1, Jira Cloud, S3 store; the ADP project). A bound local ticket that is deleted or archived classifies TERMINAL and binding_walk emits an outbound update {status: Done} on every pass. Reproduced on origin/main and v0.13.1 with the real classify/binding_walk (evidence: .rebar/worktrees/inv-bridge-tombstone/.rebar/scratch/inv-75058/, repro.py, out-main.txt, out-v0131.txt).\n\nIntent on record: 444d-c21f-2c82-4622 (closed) states \"Approved policy: local archive/delete drives the Jira issue to a terminal status (Done)\", planned to \"optionally retire the binding after the terminal transition\", and its AC reads \"drives that issue to ... Done, or unbinds it\". Commit 4bd06245d66 built the transition and not the retirement, so the binding persists and re-closes a reopened Jira issue every pass. In ADP, 19 deleted stories are queued to close their Jira issues, held only by max_acting_fraction (19/130); ADP-41 was closed by one pass and later reopened by a person.\n\nGaps:\n- binding_walk.py hardcodes `_TERMINAL_JIRA_STATUS = \"Done\"` instead of routing through effective_status_map(), contrary to 444d's implementation contract and docs/mapping-seam.md (\"the reconciler routes each outbound status through the effective status map\"); `archived` was never added to the map; a `deleted = \"skip\"` override has no effect.\n- No supported way to retire a binding (BindingStore.unbind exists only internally; no CLI/library/MCP surface).\n- `rebar delete`/`archive` give no warning that a bound ticket will close its Jira issue; undocumented.\n\n## Plan\nPending the maintainer's policy decision on what delete/archive of a bound ticket does to Jira; the plan and acceptance criteria are written once it is made.\n\n## File impact (expected)\n- src/rebar/reconciler/binding_walk.py\n- src/rebar/reconciler/classify.py\n- src/rebar/reconciler/config.py","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"ac57-7690-8736-4cca","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Deleted or archived bound ticket keeps closing its Jira issue","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f561a670-53df-48ec-ac8c-e9e885efe565"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793340958563562668,"uuid":"da85e235-adc6-4b94-9ea6-3efb4950735f"}